// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 13-expression-semantics
// facility: [Deref] (the operand is a reference, a guard or a raw pointer); D-0254; conf.deref-simd
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.type-mismatch (static)
//
// A `simd` is a value, not a reference: `*v` is rejected before the
// program runs (it had reached `coby`'s evaluator, which faulted, and
// `cobc`'s code generator, which stopped with an internal error).

import std;

fn main()
{
    simd<f32, 4> v = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0];
    printf("%v\n", simd_sum(*v));
}
